            <ArticleTitle>The time has come to reexamine the gold standard when evaluating noninvasive testing.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>100-1, A8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Angiographically identified 50% cross-sectional narrowing of a coronary artery fails to accurately identify compromised myocardial perfusion. Noninvasive tests should be correlated with intravascular ultrasound or coronary flow reserve to determine their clinical utility.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
